# Git Commit Standards

## No Cursor co-author trailer

**Never** add this footer (or any Cursor co-author trailer) to commits:

```
Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
```

If a tool injects it automatically, strip it before finishing (amend / rewrite) so the published commit message has no `Co-authored-by: Cursor` line.

Do not add other AI co-author trailers unless the user explicitly asks.

## Language

Match this repository’s recent commit style: **Chinese** subject/body is preferred (see `git log`). Keep conventional-commit `type(scope):` prefixes.

### Format

```
type(scope?): subject

body?

footer?
```

### Length Limits

- Subject line: concise (aim ≤ 72 chars; keep readable)
- Body: wrap around 72 chars when practical
- Total commit message: keep focused; avoid noise

### Types

- `feat`: New feature
- `fix`: Bug fix
- `docs`: Documentation changes
- `style`: Code style changes
- `refactor`: Code refactoring
- `perf`: Performance improvements
- `test`: Adding/updating tests
- `chore`: Build tasks, configs, etc

### Rules

- Subject: present tense / imperative feel, no trailing period
- Scope (optional): package or area (e.g. `pam`, `pamenv`)
- Body (optional): why and notable impact; bullets OK for multiple items
- Footer (optional): breaking changes, issue refs — **not** Cursor co-author

### Examples

```
feat(pam): 详情改用 slug，并支持删除与 CLI 环境管理

详情 URL 使用 slug；owner 可删除项目。
```

```
fix(pamenv): 修复 delete 成功却误报 API failed
```
